    in separate attributes, and js/contact.js joins them into an href on the visitor's first hover,
    focus or tap. The anchor carries no href on purpose - with JS off it is inert text rather than a
    link that goes nowhere - which is why the noscript below still has to carry the address in a
    form a human can read and retype. #}
    <a id="email-link" class="email-link" data-local="sckerk" data-domain="gmail.com">Email</a>
    <noscript>
        <span class="email-fallback">Email: sckerk [at] gmail [dot] com</span>
    </noscript>

    {# No target="_blank" here, so no rel="noopener" is needed. Noted because its absence reads like
